  "question": {
    "text": "In the figure shown, a circuit contains two identical resistors with resistance <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>&#937;</mi></math> and an inductance with <math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>.</mo></math> An ideal battery of <math><mn>15</mn><mi>V</mi></math> is connected in the circuit. What will be the current through the battery long after the switch is closed?<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0141_f8e32a32cef5.png\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5.5</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>7.5</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0141_8de1acf1d80f.png\" /><br /><br />After a long time, when the growth of current in the circuit has stopped, the inductor will work as a conductor. Therefore the effective resistance of the circuit will be,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the current through the circuit will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2.5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>A</mi></math></p>"
  }
}